WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:02.752 position:66%
I started out, you know, like a normal kid
in high school.

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:05.296 position:56%
I used to just smoke
regular flower weed with my buddies.

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:07.716
And then one of my friends
introduced me to a dab rig.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:10.802 position:56%
And it would get to the point
where I was having to smoke that pen

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:13.805
like every 30 minutes
in order to keep the high up.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:18.101 position:61%
Concerns about marijuana
used to be the stuff of Reefer Madness.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:22.439 position:63%
But in Colorado, already
a decade into legalization, high-potency

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.607
products are birthing new critics.

00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:28.319
We've had legalization here now
for a long time

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:33.241
and it has just wreaked
havoc on a generation of our kids.

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:36.244
Despite the millions in marijuana
tax revenue,

00:00:36.244 --> 00:00:39.289 position:63%
some residents feel
there have been unintended consequences.

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:43.626 position:66%
The youngest kid I've seen that's addicted
to pot is seven. It doesn't matter

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:48.465 position:63%
what kind of parent you are,
cannabis in our community is everywhere.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:52.010
For a child, it's
as simple as going on to Snapchat,

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.345
finding out where they're dealing
and going and getting it.

00:00:57.849 --> 00:00:59.559
Karen Randall is a doctor

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.520 position:63%
at a large hospital in Pueblo, Colorado.

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:06.691 position:56%
Sometimes touted as the Napa
Valley of pot, the former steel town

00:01:06.691 --> 00:01:10.028
invited the marijuana industry
in to try and boost the city.

00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:13.615 position:58%
But according to some residents,
it hasn't worked out quite like that.

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:16.493
Here it is. Like in all its glory.

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:17.827
The Napa Valley of cannabis.

00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:20.830
Yeah, that's
what the Napa Valley looks like.

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:23.958
A study in Colorado

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:27.796 position:61%
found marijuana related calls to poison
control centers more than doubled

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:31.382 position:58%
around the time recreational products
hit the market in 2014.

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:35.595 position:56%
A separate study showed vomiting
related cases in the state also rose

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:39.307
29% from 2013 to 2018.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:43.645 position:59%
One of the big ones that we see every
single day is what we call scromiting.

00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:46.731
And it's a combination
of screaming and vomiting

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:49.734
that is really kind of
peculiar to cannabis alone.

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:57.075
I would be vomiting like often.

00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:58.952
I used to weigh like 150 pounds.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.496
I got to the point
where as weighing 117 pounds.

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:02.789
So I went to my psychiatrist.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.707
He actually did a scope

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:05.125
to see

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.252 position:56%
if I had like gallbladder
cancer or something, which I didn't,

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:09.337
and there was nothing wrong with my
GI tract.

00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:11.381
He asked me, do you use substances?

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:12.549
And I said, yeah, I use marijuana.

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:16.386 position:56%
He told me that you can use too much
to the point

00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:20.265 position:59%
where it's called cannabis hyperemesis
disorder, which is where I was at.

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:24.060 position:56%
Dr. Jesse Hinckley of the University
of Colorado first became concerned

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.022 position:59%
about cannabis after seeing some youth
admitted to in-patient psychiatry.

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:31.401
These were youth typically
without any sort of previous

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:35.655 position:59%
psychiatric history
who were presenting acutely psychotic.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.825 position:56%
So hearing voices,
seeing things, paranoid, delusional.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:44.205 position:58%
And pretty abrupt onset typically
after a period of heavy cannabis use.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:49.419 position:67%
Of more than 4,000 marijuana related visits
to emergency rooms or urgent care

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:53.756
in Colorado, 5% were diagnosed
with schizophrenia or psychosis.

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:57.969
That's compared to less than 1%
among the general US population.

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:01.472
Most people don't even know
what's for sale in dispensaries.

00:03:01.472 --> 00:03:05.018
Like do you know what dabbing is
or shatter?

00:03:05.101 --> 00:03:08.813
And they make them in flavors
that are appealing to kids,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:13.693
Scooby Snacks flavored, Girl Scout
Cookie, Birthday Cake flavored.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:17.822 position:63%
Dawn Reinfeld helped form the group Blue
Rising to advocate for gun control.

00:03:17.822 --> 00:03:20.992
But they've turned their attention
toward reforming marijuana laws,

00:03:21.242 --> 00:03:23.703
the very same laws
that some of them voted for.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:27.749 position:66%
Look, if we want to say that
you need to follow the science on climate,

00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:31.502
on fracking, on Covid vaccinations,

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:36.132 position:61%
then we should be following the science
on high-potency THC.

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:39.636
But following the science
isn't as easy as it seems.

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:44.057 position:64%
There's no consensus on what level of THC
makes the product high potency.

00:03:44.182 --> 00:03:48.144 position:64%
The market is also flooded with synthetic
variations confusing matters further.

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:51.147
Raw flower

00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:54.984 position:61%
usually starts at 20% THC or higher, up
steeply

00:03:54.984 --> 00:03:57.946
from the 4% levels of yesteryear.

00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:03.159
Concentrated products
like vape rarely start below 60%.

00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:07.288 position:63%
Many extracts like dab, wax, and shatter
go above 90.

00:04:08.122 --> 00:04:09.624
It was my birthday party actually ,

00:04:09.624 --> 00:04:12.627 position:66%
so I took a dab and that was about 75% THC

00:04:12.627 --> 00:04:13.211
the first time.

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:15.838
And then eventually I found out
that I could just get to dab

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:19.550 position:67%
pen which would last me longer and in turn,
be cheaper. So two years of

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.553
just daily use at 98% THC.

00:04:23.554 --> 00:04:26.140 position:58%
Recreational marijuana is legal in 23

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:29.269 position:59%
states,
but remains illegal under federal law.

00:04:29.519 --> 00:04:30.019
The US

00:04:30.019 --> 00:04:31.896 position:56%
government is gathering data towards

00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:35.733
a pledge to reconsider legalizing
by the end of 2023.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:39.821 position:66%
While Germany is also drafting regulations
to start recreational use.

00:04:40.071 --> 00:04:42.573
I asked our hospital
how much it would cost

00:04:42.573 --> 00:04:45.618
just to see a patient get IV fluids
and some medicines.

00:04:45.827 --> 00:04:50.081 position:80%
It would be about 5 - 6,000 dollars for a ER visit.

00:04:50.081 --> 00:04:51.624
We see at least one a day.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:56.504
So if you go, okay,
that's $5,000 times 365 days.

00:04:56.504 --> 00:04:58.881
That's $1.8 million.

00:04:58.881 --> 00:05:02.260
And then if you times it by
25 ERs in Colorado,

00:05:03.344 --> 00:05:04.679
that's millions of

00:05:04.679 --> 00:05:08.599 position:59%
dollars. Spent on just the scromiting-
Just on scromiting alone.

00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:10.435
Treatment

00:05:10.435 --> 00:05:14.063
for America's drug habit often
comes down to mental health care,

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:17.150
which sometimes isn't covered
by private insurance.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:21.362 position:61%
Many such patients rely on Medicaid.
We're just cost shifting right? They’re

00:05:21.362 --> 00:05:22.196
taking money in

00:05:22.196 --> 00:05:25.575 position:64%
and we're cost shifting
their medical care to the general public.

00:05:25.575 --> 00:05:29.579 position:64%
If you look at the trends in the numbers,
not only did cannabis go up, and the

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.789
industry will say, well,
of course it went up

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:33.708
because now it's legal
and everybody's using.

00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:35.543
But methamphetamines went up.

00:05:35.543 --> 00:05:38.504
Cocaine went up. Opiates went up.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:41.591
And my test doesn't test
for fentanyl and of course

00:05:41.591 --> 00:05:44.594 position:56%
fenranyl has gone up. We're reaching
the record number of deaths.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:48.681
January 2022 Colorado
started using a tracking system

00:05:48.806 --> 00:05:52.310
that limited daily THC concentrates
per customer.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:56.314 position:59%
The compromise reached by legislators,
Blue Rising, doctors,

00:05:56.314 --> 00:05:59.776
and the local cannabis
industry had immediate impact.

00:06:00.151 --> 00:06:04.989 position:64%
Medical marijuana sales fell
about $7 million. Overall marijuana sales

00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:09.952 position:66%
also contracted,
falling about 44% below their peak of $226

00:06:09.952 --> 00:06:13.790
million in 2020.
You know, it's legal here.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.375
It's going to stay legal.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:18.920 position:66%
But how can we have a regulatory framework
that protects

00:06:19.128 --> 00:06:23.007 position:63%
public health. For the legal
marijuana industry, the stakes are high.

00:06:23.132 --> 00:06:27.387 position:67%
This year in the US, more
than a third of the $34 billion in expected

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:31.307 position:59%
cannabis sales will come from products
with high levels of THC.

00:06:31.432 --> 00:06:31.891
The US

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:34.977
Cannabis Council says
millions of Americans regularly

00:06:34.977 --> 00:06:37.980
consume marijuana products
without any issues.

00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:42.151 position:61%
Confusingly, some studies have shown
that marijuana can have both beneficial

00:06:42.151 --> 00:06:45.154
and detrimental effects
on some mental health conditions.

00:06:45.446 --> 00:06:48.616
But the industry can't deny
that the legal market has created

00:06:48.616 --> 00:06:51.619 position:58%
a new breed of supercharged products.

00:06:51.786 --> 00:06:56.707 position:59%
I honestly believe that if we had left
cannabis at the previous potency,

00:06:56.707 --> 00:06:59.710
if they had left it at 2 to 3%,
we probably wouldn't be talking.

